x-celigo-ai-guidance:
The referenced API resource exposed by this MCP tool must exist,
belong to the same user, and be of type "builder";
script-type APIs are not supported.

Reference an existing Celigo Storage file id (see GET /v1/storage/items);
folder ids and unknown ids fail with 422 "mcp_server_file_not_found",
and the same file id may appear only once across resources[].

approvedDefinitionHash.description:
Hash of the upstream definition an administrator last approved. Set
and re-pinned by any PUT that includes `upstreamMcpConnections`;
absent until the row has been matched to a discovered definition.

keyResolver.description:
Whose allowance the limit tracks. Omit it (or send endpoint) for a
server-level limit and send consumer for a per-user rate limit;
quotas accept endpoint only.
